      "title": "php2shell (CVE-2026-109618 and CVE-2026-109619) – PHP critical vulnerability fixes available",
      "hook_fa": "این خبر چه تغییری برای کاربران لینوکس ایجاد می‌کند؟",
      "description": "Introduction Two critical security vulnerabilities affecting PHP have been identified that result in unauthenticated remote code execution (RCE) for any PHP application. The vulnerabilities have been assigned the CVE-2026-109618 and CVE-2026-109619 identifiers, but are also referred to using the php2shell nickname. Ubuntu has released fixes for the affected packages for all supported releases. The two [&hellip;]",
