    "44b433e611b6": {
      "id": "44b433e611b6",
      "category": "Desktop Linux",
      "title": "OpenSUSE Leap 16.1",
      "hook_fa": "این خبر چه تغییری برای کاربران لینوکس ایجاد می‌کند؟",
      "description": "The openSUSE project has announced the release of openSUSE Leap 16.1. The release is notable for allowing both traditional installations and immutable images with transactional updates. While immutable images had previously been available for Leap Micro, they are now available across all platforms that Leap supports, including servers, desktops, and virtual machines. \"Leap's image gives the best of both for traditional and immutable users, and we expect that Tumbleweed will follow when Agama becomes the default installer for Tumbleweed as well.\" said Leap release manager Lubos Kocman. \"The Leap Micro experience people relied on is still here, but now it shares the same release, the same life cycle and the same maintenance updates as the rest of Leap, so users only have to pick the mode that fits their workload.\"",
      "score": 76,
      "source_type": "rss",
      "sources": [
        "https://lwn.net/Articles/1105131/"
      ],
      "status": "NEW",
      "approval_token": "03573aa52d944a988da0909695bef113"
